Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||10-09-2001||06:23 PM||||There once was a terrorist who thought of something so terrible, so disgusting against the USA, that as a result almost 6000 innocent civilians died. The images of two airplanes flying into the United States' largest buildings were repeated by the media over and over, until you almost had no feelings anymore watching them. Because when viewed often enough, people can get used to anything. Every now and then they would quickly tell a short story about a victim, but since these stories were of no commercial value, they were far and between.<P>The US had no other choice than to retaliate with careful planned bombings on military and political targets. Unfortunately <B>some</B> civilians were killed and some wounded. Now for some reason, the western media found it very important to give every single wounded person in Afghanistan some air-time. Presumably because they want to show off they have a reporter in a war-zone.<P>The problem with this is, is that the public now hears more sad stories about "innocent" Afghan people, than they have heared about the innocently killed and wounded in the US, shifting public opinion. In every country people are demonstrating against the "war" because innocent Afghan people are being hurt. Apparantly, they have forgotten about the 6000 dead and 10s-of-thousands of wounded civilians in the States.<P>Now the earlier mentioned terrorist is getting worried. Apparantly the target of the US attacks is to get <B>him</B>. Fortunately, he has a pre-taped message calling all muslims in the world to participate in a <B>Jihad</B>, a holy war against the US. But he has a problem. How does he reach the millions of muslims outside the middle-east? Obviously he can't give them all a call personally and not a single muslim outside the middle-east will be able to receive any tv transmissions from him. His advisor tells him not to worry. He tells him the people in the western world are such fools, they will do the work for him. So he gives the tape to Al-Jazeera, an Arabic News station. Al-Jazeera broadcasts it once. All western reporters that are able to receive the station tape it or request a copy and send it to their editors. Of course, the editors smell news and a chance to justify their fat pay-checks. So in a race to bring this "news" as an exclusive, all western news media quickly broadcast and publish Mr. Terrorist's message throughout the western world. Mr. Terrorist is suprised this is so easy and laughs his a$$ off at such stupidity. "That was the cheapest and the fastest I've ever been able to get my message across to all those muslims in the countries of my enemies" he said.<P>And he's correct. Because the western newsmedia are the most stupid people on earth.||||reg||8
Z||000001||fierospeeder||10-09-2001||06:37 PM||||I was thinking the same thing also, about the news broadcast.<P>I think its England whos having a large anti war protest going on now.<P>Bush was bitching today, that some of congress is discussing where our next moves are going to take place, and they are responsible for giving out top secret info.  <P>I always thought the news is too reviling.  Right now, we just told them were doing day attacks because its "safe" to fly during the light hours.||||reg||1
