Z||000016||84Bill||10-10-2001||09:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock: <B>Yesterday, they showed a documentary of a female journalist from London, showing the incredible monstrosities the Taliban is practicing in Afghanistan - public execution of women, the systematical killing of all men in villages, the raping of young girls, the torture of young men - all presented in "in-your-face" style. They aired this around 1 am!!! Nobody I have spoken since saw this documentary </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I watched that myself and I could not believe there could be such a barbaric government in power. The mere fact that they KILL people in an arena setting for minor acts goes against every fiber of my being. I am not a religious person by any stretch of the imagination but MY God, the God that I believe in or for that matter not even Connan's war like god "Krom" would allow this kind of act. <BR>There is only one god I know of that would delight or preach in the slaughter of men and women in public and I believe he was an outcast. <P>Thanks for your support Cliff. The US is a great country. Even though it's not perfect. There were times when things were done purely for the interests of the US government at the expense of a weaker government but this "war" is for the greater good of the world, at least I believe it is.<BR>Yeah I feel for the innocent Afghan peoples hurt in this battle of good and evil but if your stupid enough to have an anti aircraft gun on your roof because your government has put it there, well... uhh better move away quickly. Hello!<BR>Given the chance I'd rejoin the service to fight against terrorism, I feel I need to defend the freedom to live my life without fear and even more so for my children and their children. <BR>I guess as an American I have grown up used to life without terror because of the many many brave men that fought for it so many years ago. To them that died in this cause I owe my greatest gratitude and to the ones that live to this day, I can hardly stand to look straight in the eye because I have grown fat and ignorant on what they were so willing to die for.<BR>In the end it is hoped that the defender of good will win out over the evil doers and then the protestors will have something else to *****  about but at least even they will be safe from terror, even if they are to stupid (sorry songman I just had to resort to name calling  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) to realize what it took to get to that end. Much like this forum, it takes many kinds of people to make things work and you must allow for such people even if their views are not the same as yours.<P>To the younger generation, those that are 18 to late 20's. This is your fight I can't fight for you even though I want to. At 37 I can't rejoin the army in support of freedom, so you choices are clear. <P>1 Fight terrorism and maybe die for it.<BR>or<BR>2 Give up your freedoms in an increasingly restrictive world forever!<P>In the last month we have had just a taste of the restrictions to our freedom. Just imagine if an attack like Sept 11th happens again. Our country will be in a LOCKDOWN! you will not be able to move around with impunity ever again. searches and background checks will rule your world and the SS will be everywhere looking into your life like never before and it will become an excuse for the government to fight terrorism. <P>Ok I'm done kooking out for now.<BR>Thanks again Cliff<P>Heheh I must be off my rocker, painted my car red whit and blue and I'm willing to fight and god forbid die for freedom for the world at large. I'm just angry the government sees me as "to old"<BR>||||reg||1
