Z||000020||GarethWright||10-11-2001||02:33 AM||||I noticed several media-types on camera in the background during the initial broadcasts of the sept. 11th attack, you could tell them, because of all the people running to help, the media-types would stop and whip out a camera or pull escaping people aside and try to make them cry for the camera.  I saw 2 reports in particular that made me sick(I'm sure there were more) One with the reporter praising her camara man and support crew for helping her sneak past the police blockade, the other with a reporter picking through rubble in a restaurant trying for a human-interest story, something tells me He wasn't supposed to be there. Freedom of the press is guarenteed in the US, but the way its taken, reporters think they can do anything they want to. The media in general has done more harm than good for quite some time, I'm sure Saddam Hussein loved CNN or whatever during the Gulf War "There goes another flight of US bombers to where-ever, they should be there in 15 mins." gee thanks.<BR>I do agree that people need to know whats going on, but surely there could be some limits to it. <BR>||||reg||1
